36,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The data shows that a discharge call-back trial successfully reduced readmissions for elderly patients, though the effect vanished once it ended. However, shared nursing rounds faced significant practical failures, with a third of visits never completed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Our infrastructure is severely strained. Outpatient rooms and parking are full by mid-morning, and the shuttle coverage is minimal. Furthermore, the booking system only tracks named slots, meaning any flexible or unbooked work effectively disappears from our reports.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are courting disaster if we rely on external partnerships or joint ventures. I've found that joint clinics collapse over rota disputes, and data agreements with outside surgeries are a bureaucratic nightmare, taking over a year to finalize.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I'm worried about our staff! We have nine unfilled nursing posts and are spending more on agency cover. Also, while physiotherapists are leaving for the city, the midwifery team actually has some unusual slack in their rota.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are facing a delicate balance. Our budget is tighter than expected, and we must be mindful that services provided outside our walls bring no financial return to the hospital. We must choose wisely.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, the slack in midwifery staffing is an interesting point. Given the failures of shared nursing rounds and the lack of funding for off-site visits, we should prioritize programs that are sustainable and internally manageable.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, I agree. Any program requiring additional outpatient space or complex scheduling will likely fail or go unrecorded. We must avoid adding pressure to an already saturated physical and digital infrastructure.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, your point on the booking system is particularly poignant. If we implement a program that doesn't fit into a named slot, it will simply vanish from the records, rendering any perceived success invisible to the board.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, that sounds so scary! We can't let the hard work of our friends just disappear. Maybe we should look for something that fits into those slots or uses the slack in the midwifery team?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see you all supporting one another. We must seek a path that honors our staff's well-being while remaining financially honest. A program that generates no revenue and drains a shrinking budget may be a kindness today, but a burden tomorrow.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, your point on revenue is critical. Since off-site visits bring no tariff and our budget is shrinking, we should avoid programs that rely heavily on home visits or external coordination.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, exactly. If we cannot find a room and the booking system cannot track the activity, the program is a ghost. We need something that utilizes existing slack without requiring new physical space.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, it seems we are in agreement. We must avoid the siren song of ""external coordination"" and ""joint ventures,"" as the bureaucracy and rota disputes would likely dismantle the program before it ever matured.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I agree! We should definitely avoid anything that makes our already tired nurses even more stressed. If the midwifery team has some extra time, maybe we can find a way to help them lead something?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is wise to align our ambitions with our reality. Let us look for a path that utilizes our existing strengths and available time, ensuring the program can breathe and grow without suffocating our staff or our finances.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We have established that we must avoid off-site visits, external data dependencies, and programs that strain our limited physical space or nursing staff. We should look for a candidate that utilizes the midwifery slack and fits our internal constraints.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I concur. We need a program that is internally contained, avoids the saturated outpatient rooms, and leverages the available midwifery capacity. Any proposal requiring external agreements or home visits is simply not viable given our current constraints.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we have collectively built a very restrictive filter. We require a program that is internally managed, avoids the bureaucratic quagmire of external agreements, and utilizes existing staffing slack rather than adding to the nursing deficit.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so glad we're all thinking about the staff! Let's hope one of the candidates fits perfectly so we can help our patients without making anyone too tired. I'm ready to see the options!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Servas,,The clarity we have achieved together is a testament to your diligence. We now possess a mirror reflecting our true capacity; let us use it to choose a path of genuine sustainability. I am ready.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
